  "body": "The [nuke-room-from-db.sh](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/scripts-dev/nuke-room-from-db.sh) script doesn't nuke the room from **communities**\r\nif you added a room into a community on the lefthandside and then nuke that room, it is still in the list of rooms in the community\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- using **postgresql** use the [nuke-room-from-db.sh](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/scripts-dev/nuke-room-from-db.sh) script on the room\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: my own homeserver\r\n- **Version**:       0.28.0\r\n- **Install method**: git clone/pip      \r\n- **Platform**:       \r\n  -  Debian squeeze version 9.3\r\n  - Hardware: Intel Core™ i7-6700 Quad-Core (Hetzner EX41S),  running in a XEN vm/container (xen 4.6)\r\n- Version of riot-web: 0.14.2\r\n\r\n",
